1
00:00:26,569 --> 00:00:33,492
PARTICIPANTS WISHING TO
REVEAL THEIR FEELINGS

2
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:43,377
WILL MAKE THEIR CONFESSIONS
AT THE BUS STOP

3
00:00:45,546 --> 00:00:51,677
IF THE CONFESSION IS ACCEPTABLE,

4
00:00:53,262 --> 00:01:00,186
THE TWO WILL BOARD THE BUS TOGETHER
TO TRANSIT

5
00:01:03,397 --> 00:01:07,443
Love Transit 35+.
It's finally time for final confessions.

6
00:01:10,112 --> 00:01:12,281
Here we are. The moment of truth.

7
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:15,075
This is the final confession,

8
00:01:15,159 --> 00:01:17,369
but it doesn't mean
it's all romantic declarations.

9
00:01:17,703 --> 00:01:19,371
For some, this might just be

10
00:01:19,455 --> 00:01:22,124
a chance to say thank you
or bid a final farewell.

11
00:01:23,209 --> 00:01:26,128
So a chance to get stuff
off their chest, right?

12
00:01:26,212 --> 00:01:28,297
Exactly. So, how do you feel?

13
00:01:28,422 --> 00:01:31,759
On that last night, Ryo was all like,

14
00:01:31,842 --> 00:01:34,595
"I've unlocked romance mode!"

15
00:01:34,678 --> 00:01:36,472
He did.

16
00:01:36,555 --> 00:01:37,848
He was saying that.

17
00:01:37,932 --> 00:01:39,099
And he had

18
00:01:39,433 --> 00:01:41,101
his top two picks, Mao and Misato,

19
00:01:41,185 --> 00:01:43,395
sitting on either side of him.

20
00:01:43,479 --> 00:01:44,563
Which one would it be?

21
00:01:44,647 --> 00:01:46,440
Hard to say what he meant by that.

22
00:01:46,524 --> 00:01:50,528
But Ryo's bound to make some kind of move

23
00:01:50,611 --> 00:01:52,655
on confession day.

24
00:01:52,738 --> 00:01:54,031
For sure.

25
00:01:54,406 --> 00:01:55,616
And Daichi…

26
00:01:55,699 --> 00:01:57,201
he's probably going to confess to Kaede.

27
00:01:57,326 --> 00:01:58,702
Yes.

28
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:02,122
I think he has a chance.

29
00:02:02,331 --> 00:02:04,750
Alright Anne-san,

30
00:02:04,834 --> 00:02:07,545
mind doing the honors
and rolling the final clip?

31
00:02:08,212 --> 00:02:11,382
Now that their long hocance
has come to an end…

32
00:02:11,674 --> 00:02:14,009
What kind of Love Transit choices
will these exes make?

33
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:16,971
Watch as these ten adults make
the most defining

34
00:02:17,054 --> 00:02:18,848
decisions of their lives.

35
00:02:23,894 --> 00:02:25,062
Who's this?

36
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:28,190
Who's going first? Who is this?

37
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:29,191
Who?

38
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,821
It's Kanako.

39
00:03:25,289 --> 00:03:27,625
Good morning.

40
00:03:33,464 --> 00:03:34,965
Were you surprised?

41
00:03:35,341 --> 00:03:36,592
Yeah, I was.

42
00:03:36,675 --> 00:03:39,261
You were? I see.

43
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:48,020
Hika-chan… now that it's been a week,

44
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:50,439
isn't this hocance kind of suffocating?

45
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:52,524
Hocance? It's brutal.

46
00:03:52,608 --> 00:03:55,361
Right? Me too…

47
00:03:56,403 --> 00:03:58,364
it's been really tough.

48
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:00,658
Even though I love everyone here.

49
00:04:00,741 --> 00:04:03,452
I genuinely love every single one of them.

50
00:04:03,535 --> 00:04:06,997
You're at your absolute best when you're
just being unapologetically you.

51
00:04:07,081 --> 00:04:09,416
Really? But I'm stubborn as hell.

52
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:11,001
Who cares?

53
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:12,753
Anyone who hates that about you

54
00:04:12,836 --> 00:04:15,047
just isn't your type.
Why bend over backwards for them?

55
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:16,465
Yeah… you're right.

56
00:04:16,757 --> 00:04:22,262
He held me up when the stay got brutal,

57
00:04:22,846 --> 00:04:26,433
and told me I was actually genuine.

58
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:29,603
I realized, "Wow, he really sees me."

59
00:04:30,688 --> 00:04:32,272
That's when I let my guard down.

60
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:36,193
I just want to tell Hika-chan
how grateful I am.

61
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:38,946
So it's a thank-you,
not a romance confession.

62
00:04:39,238 --> 00:04:45,202
Looking back at how I acted,
I was so immature.

63
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:47,246
Honestly, it's embarrassing.

64
00:04:50,249 --> 00:04:53,752
You kept checking in on me,

65
00:04:54,795 --> 00:04:57,339
and weren't afraid to call me out

66
00:04:57,965 --> 00:05:01,885
when I was out of line.
I'm so grateful for that.

67
00:05:07,016 --> 00:05:09,977
I've actually grown since day one.

68
00:05:10,352 --> 00:05:11,562
Wouldn't you say?

69
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:18,736
And back in the car,

70
00:05:19,028 --> 00:05:21,947
you kept repeating,
"I don't deserve love,"

71
00:05:22,364 --> 00:05:25,576
"I don't deserve happiness."

72
00:05:25,701 --> 00:05:28,078
That's complete bullshit.

73
00:05:28,954 --> 00:05:33,792
You do deserve love.
You do deserve to be happy.

74
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:39,339
I just feel like…

75
00:05:39,423 --> 00:05:41,925
I don't get to be happy until
Mao finds her happiness first.

76
00:05:42,342 --> 00:05:44,636
I can't help but think like that.

77
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:48,432
So you and Mao both can't be happy?

78
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,142
That's how I feel.

79
00:05:50,225 --> 00:05:52,686
That's not true…

80
00:05:53,604 --> 00:05:55,314
He's always carrying

81
00:05:55,439 --> 00:05:58,192
this weird complex,
like he has to make Mao happy,

82
00:05:58,358 --> 00:06:01,361
or he can't cause trouble for Mao.

83
00:06:02,154 --> 00:06:03,655
He deserves to be happy, too.

84
00:06:03,822 --> 00:06:06,200
Everyone's happier if Hika-chan's happy.

85
00:06:06,283 --> 00:06:11,038
That's the mindset
I really wanted to break him out of.

86
00:06:11,497 --> 00:06:13,916
If you leave this hocance

87
00:06:14,083 --> 00:06:16,877
the exact same guy who walked in…

88
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:20,589
we came here hoping to change, right?

89
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:22,841
So…

90
00:06:23,675 --> 00:06:26,637
let's make sure
it's a step in the right direction.

91
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:32,559
I want you to keep being genuinely happy.

92
00:06:35,813 --> 00:06:38,357
If you're happy,

93
00:06:38,607 --> 00:06:42,319
I know Mao and the kids will be happy too.

94
00:06:42,444 --> 00:06:44,363
And so will I.

95
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:53,038
Thank you for coming into my life.

96
00:06:53,247 --> 00:06:55,499
Thanks for being such a real friend to me.

97
00:07:05,425 --> 00:07:07,010
Man…

98
00:07:11,181 --> 00:07:12,724
Thank you.

99
00:07:13,183 --> 00:07:15,018
Thank you.

100
00:07:16,311 --> 00:07:20,816
If it had just been me and Mao

101
00:07:21,608 --> 00:07:24,486
stuck together for a month,

102
00:07:27,322 --> 00:07:29,575
I don't think I ever would've changed.

103
00:07:32,870 --> 00:07:37,541
Everyone showed me how to actually open up

104
00:07:37,749 --> 00:07:41,086
and wear my heart on my sleeve…

105
00:07:41,170 --> 00:07:43,672
especially you, Kanako.

106
00:07:46,091 --> 00:07:52,806
So I'm gonna go give Mao a real apology

107
00:07:55,142 --> 00:07:57,644
and lay all my feelings on the line.

108
00:08:04,151 --> 00:08:06,445
I guess it's time for me to go.

109
00:08:07,446 --> 00:08:08,530
Do your best.

110
00:08:08,614 --> 00:08:09,489
Seriously…

111
00:08:11,867 --> 00:08:13,160
thank you for crossing my path.

112
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:14,620
Thank you, too.

113
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,749
Thank you.

114
00:08:18,957 --> 00:08:20,417
I really want to hug you right now,

115
00:08:21,752 --> 00:08:23,503
but I know how you are with boundaries…

116
00:08:24,588 --> 00:08:25,756
Bye.

117
00:08:25,839 --> 00:08:27,174
Thanks.

118
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:57,621
Good luck. Bye. Thank you.

119
00:09:03,418 --> 00:09:06,046
He held me up so much during this trip.

120
00:09:06,255 --> 00:09:09,216
A million thank-yous wouldn't be enough,

121
00:09:11,301 --> 00:09:13,512
but I'm just glad I got to tell him.

122
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:18,892
Thanks to Satoshi
inviting me on this stay,

123
00:09:19,685 --> 00:09:23,188
I got to discover a side of myself
I never knew existed.

124
00:09:23,981 --> 00:09:27,359
It gave me a chance to really step back
and reflect on everything.

125
00:09:28,402 --> 00:09:29,778
I had an amazing time.

126
00:09:32,239 --> 00:09:34,741
Man, watching Kanako…

127
00:09:35,033 --> 00:09:38,328
at first, she was so furious

128
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:41,456
and going through so much pain.

129
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:45,502
It really makes you root for her to
find real love again down the road.

130
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:48,547
Writing out cheat sheets like that
feels like a romantic confession,

131
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:51,800
but having so much to say to a friend…

132
00:09:51,883 --> 00:09:54,928
and writing it all down
so thoughtfully was just so sweet.

133
00:09:55,012 --> 00:09:56,972
She really is such a wonderful girl.

134
00:09:57,222 --> 00:09:58,974
Kanako, thank you so much.

135
00:11:01,119 --> 00:11:03,205
Alright, I'm ready.

136
00:11:08,126 --> 00:11:10,796
Hey, good morning.

137
00:11:11,254 --> 00:11:12,756
Good morning.

138
00:11:13,298 --> 00:11:14,299
What's with the leopard print?

139
00:11:14,466 --> 00:11:16,510
This is Misato. What kind of confession?

140
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:18,011
Mind if I sit here?

141
00:11:18,261 --> 00:11:19,304
You actually carry a handkerchief?

142
00:11:19,388 --> 00:11:20,222
Of course.

143
00:11:20,347 --> 00:11:21,807
You had it every single day?

144
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:23,392
I did.

145
00:11:31,650 --> 00:11:35,445
My mind's already made up on one person.

146
00:11:38,365 --> 00:11:39,783
Need me to give you a push?

147
00:11:39,866 --> 00:11:42,077
No, well…

148
00:11:47,707 --> 00:11:49,835
give me a second.

149
00:11:52,295 --> 00:11:54,381
I'm not crying, alright?

150
00:11:59,970 --> 00:12:01,972
I'm definitely not crying.

151
00:12:09,896 --> 00:12:12,190
Man, this ocean breeze is
stinging my eyes.

152
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:16,653
So, I mean,

153
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:20,991
when you invited me out for drinks
about twice last year…

154
00:12:22,409 --> 00:12:23,743
I was like, "For real?"

155
00:12:23,952 --> 00:12:26,872
"There's gotta be better guys out there."

156
00:12:27,914 --> 00:12:30,125
'Cuz back then,

157
00:12:31,376 --> 00:12:35,297
I totally saw us as really good friends.

158
00:12:36,173 --> 00:12:38,633
So I was actually planning on
playing wingman.

159
00:12:38,717 --> 00:12:40,802
That was my main mindset going in.

160
00:12:41,928 --> 00:12:43,680
But…

161
00:12:45,182 --> 00:12:49,144
Seeing how you haven't changed one bit,

162
00:12:50,145 --> 00:12:51,771
you know?

163
00:12:52,564 --> 00:12:55,567
I mean, getting that completely smashed

164
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:58,570
in front of total strangers?
That's insane.

165
00:12:58,653 --> 00:13:02,991
It's a genuine talent.
It just reminded me all over again…

166
00:13:03,658 --> 00:13:06,745
that's the stuff I really fell for.

167
00:13:06,912 --> 00:13:08,330
Right.

168
00:13:10,874 --> 00:13:14,044
And I realized,

169
00:13:15,837 --> 00:13:17,631
this time for sure,

170
00:13:19,174 --> 00:13:22,010
I want to treat you right.

171
00:13:24,429 --> 00:13:26,097
Ocean breeze…

172
00:13:30,393 --> 00:13:32,062
Thank you.

173
00:13:36,650 --> 00:13:38,151
Pass me that handkerchief for a second.

174
00:13:39,486 --> 00:13:41,821
The ocean breeze is getting in my eyes.

175
00:13:41,905 --> 00:13:43,657
Isn't that what I'm supposed to do?

176
00:13:44,699 --> 00:13:46,576
I'm telling you,
it's the damn ocean breeze.

177
00:13:49,746 --> 00:13:53,416
And you know how we reconnected

178
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:57,087
after all those years?

179
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,463
Yeah.

180
00:13:58,672 --> 00:14:01,049
Pretty sure I'm the one
who reached out first.

181
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:02,884
Right.

182
00:14:02,968 --> 00:14:08,056
Guess you were always
in the back of my mind.

183
00:14:13,645 --> 00:14:15,564
My mind's made up.

184
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:18,984
It's set.

185
00:14:19,234 --> 00:14:24,447
Turns out my heart's still with my X.

186
00:14:24,698 --> 00:14:28,118
Maybe my first love is
supposed to be my last.

187
00:14:29,369 --> 00:14:31,121
So…

188
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:35,166
whether it means dating or marriage,
I don't know…

189
00:14:37,168 --> 00:14:39,504
but part of me

190
00:14:41,298 --> 00:14:42,716
just wants to ask you

191
00:14:42,799 --> 00:14:46,511
to be my girl again.

192
00:14:46,678 --> 00:14:49,055
I'm all locked in.

193
00:14:52,017 --> 00:14:54,853
I know I have to face you

194
00:14:55,812 --> 00:15:01,693
and talk things through properly.

195
00:15:02,611 --> 00:15:07,282
I just want to do it right this time
and really treasure you.

196
00:15:11,578 --> 00:15:14,998
So yeah… if you feel up for it,

197
00:15:15,332 --> 00:15:18,376
maybe we take that bus back together.

198
00:15:19,878 --> 00:15:22,339
That's where my heart's at.

199
00:15:24,549 --> 00:15:26,134
Okay.

200
00:15:37,812 --> 00:15:40,148
First off…

201
00:15:41,066 --> 00:15:44,486
this whole hocance thing?

202
00:15:45,028 --> 00:15:48,031
Totally not your style,

203
00:15:48,823 --> 00:15:52,869
but thank you for coming.

204
00:15:54,162 --> 00:15:55,997
I just wanted to say that.

205
00:15:56,414 --> 00:16:00,293
I figured you'd be like,

206
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:03,546
"Why are you bringing up pet peeves

207
00:16:04,464 --> 00:16:09,928
from over 20 years ago now?"

208
00:16:10,136 --> 00:16:14,474
But you actually sat there
and listened to me.

209
00:16:14,849 --> 00:16:17,102
Like, "I really need to step up."

210
00:16:18,436 --> 00:16:22,607
And that really hit me…

211
00:16:24,567 --> 00:16:26,569
because honestly, I didn't expect

212
00:16:26,653 --> 00:16:30,240
you to be someone
I could be this raw and honest with.

213
00:16:31,574 --> 00:16:34,703
When we talked by the pool,

214
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:38,707
I was so happy…

215
00:16:39,749 --> 00:16:44,045
but part of me kept worrying

216
00:16:44,421 --> 00:16:46,423
if I was pushing you too hard.

217
00:16:46,548 --> 00:16:50,427
I was the one who asked you to change,

218
00:16:51,219 --> 00:16:55,056
but then I thought
it'd become a heavy burden on you.

219
00:16:56,683 --> 00:17:03,690
And I started wondering
if we were better off as good friends…

220
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:10,447
or if I was just letting my own fear
keep me from

221
00:17:11,406 --> 00:17:17,287
taking that step forward again.

222
00:17:20,331 --> 00:17:23,668
I see. Well…

223
00:17:24,461 --> 00:17:27,505
I'm used to riding solo anyway.

224
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:31,217
So you don't need to
worry about me at all.

225
00:17:32,343 --> 00:17:34,179
Just know…

226
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,307
I'm rooting for you.

227
00:17:43,605 --> 00:17:46,775
Alright, see ya around.

228
00:18:39,244 --> 00:18:41,371
I'm gonna trust you one more time.

229
00:18:45,708 --> 00:18:47,710
Maybe I'll give it one more shot.

230
00:18:47,836 --> 00:18:49,087
Oh, yeah?

231
00:18:51,172 --> 00:18:53,049
Thank you.

232
00:18:53,842 --> 00:18:55,844
So… shall we head back?

233
00:18:56,052 --> 00:18:57,929
Yeah, let's go.

234
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:03,434
Honestly, I was struggling with
what to do right up until the last second.

235
00:19:05,186 --> 00:19:06,521
How was the date?

236
00:19:06,604 --> 00:19:09,023
It was fun.

237
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:13,027
He asked me, "If we got back together,
where would you wanna travel?"

238
00:19:13,361 --> 00:19:14,988
He did?

239
00:19:15,071 --> 00:19:16,322
I like that question.

240
00:19:16,531 --> 00:19:19,576
I could picture it, and it sounded fun.

241
00:19:19,951 --> 00:19:23,329
Well… I like Thailand.

242
00:19:24,831 --> 00:19:26,666
Crap, I don't have a passport.

243
00:19:29,919 --> 00:19:34,173
I can see us having a good time, but…

244
00:19:34,799 --> 00:19:38,970
part of me worries we'll just fall back
into the same old mistakes.

245
00:19:39,512 --> 00:19:42,807
You really suit each other.

246
00:19:42,891 --> 00:19:47,478
Your vibes are on the same wavelength.

247
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:51,524
What should I do?

248
00:19:54,277 --> 00:19:58,364
My own issues… like my inability to trust?

249
00:19:58,656 --> 00:20:02,619
I really want to work through that.

250
00:20:07,582 --> 00:20:10,001
Think of our relationship like

251
00:20:10,126 --> 00:20:14,547
a set of completely
rusted-out train tracks.

252
00:20:15,757 --> 00:20:17,842
We never actually
talked things out back then.

253
00:20:18,092 --> 00:20:22,263
By having real arguments now, we're slowly

254
00:20:22,347 --> 00:20:24,057
repairing those rusted tracks.

255
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:26,893
And maybe…

256
00:20:26,976 --> 00:20:29,354
they'll turn into a smooth,
clean track again.

257
00:20:30,438 --> 00:20:33,775
Maybe they'll end up
even stronger than before.

258
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:35,652
Right?

259
00:20:39,447 --> 00:20:42,617
It made me want to give it another shot.

260
00:20:42,992 --> 00:20:45,370
That's why I took the bus.

261
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:47,580
Okay, then… thanks.

262
00:20:47,664 --> 00:20:49,082
Yup.

263
00:20:52,919 --> 00:20:55,213
Man, this is so embarrassing.

264
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:06,307
I won't be delivering Jump
and beer to you anymore.

265
00:21:06,391 --> 00:21:08,434
I buy my beer by the crate now.

266
00:21:08,893 --> 00:21:09,894
Whole crates.

267
00:21:10,061 --> 00:21:11,104
You've grown up.

268
00:21:11,187 --> 00:21:12,313
All grown up.

269
00:21:13,856 --> 00:21:16,818
Next time, let's hit up Odaiba,
go to the aquarium…

270
00:21:17,151 --> 00:21:19,153
somewhere far away
from the salty ocean breeze.

271
00:21:29,956 --> 00:21:31,124
They made it official.

272
00:21:31,207 --> 00:21:32,750
Misato and Ryo.

273
00:21:32,834 --> 00:21:35,420
A successful Love Transit couple.

274
00:21:35,628 --> 00:21:38,214
Misato and Ryo have successfully completed
their love transit.

275
00:21:38,297 --> 00:21:42,844
Ryo's currently working in Fukui

276
00:21:42,927 --> 00:21:44,721
while Misato's based in Tokyo.

277
00:21:44,804 --> 00:21:46,389
They are doing long-distance.

278
00:21:46,472 --> 00:21:47,348
Oh, she's in Tokyo.

279
00:21:47,432 --> 00:21:48,683
It's long-distance now.

280
00:21:48,766 --> 00:21:52,603
After the final confession,
they took photo booth pics in Tokyo,

281
00:21:52,687 --> 00:21:54,564
recreating the exact same pose they did

282
00:21:54,647 --> 00:21:57,608
20 years ago. Take a look.

283
00:21:57,859 --> 00:21:59,986
The one on the left is from 20 years ago,

284
00:22:00,069 --> 00:22:02,697
and they re-created it on the right.

285
00:22:02,780 --> 00:22:04,073
They look so happy.

286
00:22:04,282 --> 00:22:06,117
Starting out long-distance might actually

287
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:08,161
be a blessing in disguise for them.

288
00:22:08,244 --> 00:22:10,163
Just the right amount of space.

289
00:22:22,967 --> 00:22:24,052
Isn't that Daichi?

290
00:22:24,135 --> 00:22:26,429
It's Daichi.

291
00:22:28,014 --> 00:22:30,141
I was curious about these two.

292
00:23:19,857 --> 00:23:21,651
Sorry to keep you waiting.

293
00:23:24,737 --> 00:23:27,740
Was it hot out here? Are you alright?

294
00:23:36,707 --> 00:23:38,918
Over this past month,

295
00:23:39,001 --> 00:23:41,671
I got to see so many
different sides of you.

296
00:23:43,631 --> 00:23:47,218
Sides of you I'd never seen before.

297
00:23:47,802 --> 00:23:52,390
I realized you carry

298
00:23:52,682 --> 00:23:54,475
deeper love and warmth

299
00:23:54,559 --> 00:23:57,061
inside you than anyone else.

300
00:23:58,312 --> 00:24:00,940
When we went on that special date,

301
00:24:01,274 --> 00:24:03,985
I'd never seen
a sunrise that breathtaking.

302
00:24:05,236 --> 00:24:10,116
And first time seeing you get
so pure and genuinely excited…

303
00:24:13,953 --> 00:24:17,373
For the past six years,
I lived with this mindset

304
00:24:17,498 --> 00:24:21,043
that as long as you're happy,

305
00:24:21,127 --> 00:24:23,713
that's all that matters.

306
00:24:24,964 --> 00:24:28,634
But that basically
became a wall between us.

307
00:24:31,387 --> 00:24:33,306
And…

308
00:24:34,473 --> 00:24:37,351
I realized that I had to figure out

309
00:24:37,602 --> 00:24:39,395
what I actually wanted for myself.

310
00:24:49,447 --> 00:24:51,240
Are you glad you came here?

311
00:24:55,328 --> 00:25:00,791
For me… well,

312
00:25:00,958 --> 00:25:04,170
Do you actually see me as a woman?

313
00:25:12,803 --> 00:25:16,182
You never really crossed
that line with me,

314
00:25:17,600 --> 00:25:19,894
so I felt like

315
00:25:19,977 --> 00:25:22,271
you were walking on eggshells…

316
00:25:22,355 --> 00:25:24,607
trying way too hard to be considerate.

317
00:25:27,735 --> 00:25:32,448
I want more masculine energy.

318
00:25:36,535 --> 00:25:39,664
But I also realized
that was your way of showing kindness.

319
00:25:40,957 --> 00:25:42,875
That's why I came here to start.

320
00:25:50,716 --> 00:25:54,345
During the rest of this stay,

321
00:25:55,346 --> 00:25:57,723
just try to picture it.

322
00:25:59,350 --> 00:26:01,435
What it'd be like if we got back together.

323
00:26:02,937 --> 00:26:04,855
If we gave it another shot.

324
00:26:08,943 --> 00:26:11,445
My answer is…

325
00:26:12,571 --> 00:26:16,742
Staying friends isn't an option for me.

326
00:26:19,745 --> 00:26:22,540
We will be together forever.

327
00:26:23,249 --> 00:26:27,712
That's my answer.

328
00:26:37,722 --> 00:26:41,684
I realized I've always seen you
as a woman.

329
00:26:43,352 --> 00:26:45,855
I'm deeply in love with you.

330
00:26:49,483 --> 00:26:51,402
No matter what comes our way,

331
00:26:54,363 --> 00:26:56,365
I know we can pull through

332
00:26:57,325 --> 00:26:59,118
together.

333
00:27:04,123 --> 00:27:07,960
I can give you that romantic spark
you're looking for.

334
00:27:17,011 --> 00:27:19,263
Please… give us another shot.

335
00:27:33,152 --> 00:27:37,198
I could tell you were putting
so much real thought

336
00:27:37,281 --> 00:27:39,867
into this.

337
00:27:40,159 --> 00:27:45,081
First off, I was genuinely happy
that you came here.

338
00:27:46,332 --> 00:27:49,210
And I poured my heart out
about so much, right?

339
00:27:49,960 --> 00:27:52,671
Like when I asked
if you actually saw me as a woman.

340
00:27:52,755 --> 00:27:53,839
Yeah.

341
00:27:57,885 --> 00:28:01,263
And you really faced that head-on.

342
00:28:05,226 --> 00:28:08,562
I still hold so much affection for you.

343
00:28:10,231 --> 00:28:15,319
The way you look at me…
it's so incredibly sweet.

344
00:28:24,578 --> 00:28:28,916
It feels like forever since we held hands.
Maybe since the sunrise date?

345
00:28:29,250 --> 00:28:31,127
-That's wrong.
-Yeah, it is.

346
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:32,878
We held hands on the beach.

347
00:28:35,339 --> 00:28:37,466
You shut that down fast.

348
00:28:38,801 --> 00:28:40,553
Alright then.

349
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:44,056
I'll be waiting.

350
00:29:22,970 --> 00:29:24,472
Yes or no?

351
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:26,974
Which way?

352
00:29:27,391 --> 00:29:28,851
Is she getting on?

353
00:30:18,859 --> 00:30:20,402
She didn't board the bus.

354
00:31:12,413 --> 00:31:15,666
He'll always be someone
deeply important to me,

355
00:31:20,004 --> 00:31:21,755
but…

356
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:25,759
when you asked me to picture
our future back at the hotel,

357
00:31:25,968 --> 00:31:29,888
the fact that I just couldn't
visualize it… that was everything.

358
00:31:43,277 --> 00:31:46,405
We both came here looking for
an all-or-nothing answer.

359
00:32:38,415 --> 00:32:40,334
Don't cry.

360
00:32:52,971 --> 00:32:54,807
You put so much thought into this.

361
00:33:02,439 --> 00:33:05,567
It just terrifies me…

362
00:33:07,194 --> 00:33:09,113
picturing a life without you.

363
00:33:09,446 --> 00:33:14,201
Just thinking about how much
it's gonna hurt… I can't stop crying.

364
00:33:21,875 --> 00:33:23,544
Thank you for everything.

365
00:33:31,510 --> 00:33:34,096
Thinking this is goodbye for good…

366
00:33:34,638 --> 00:33:38,809
I couldn't watch the bus pull away.

367
00:33:42,563 --> 00:33:46,692
We talked so much this past month,
but even after all that,

368
00:33:47,025 --> 00:33:49,236
that romantic spark,

369
00:33:49,319 --> 00:33:52,781
seeing him as a partner again,
just wasn't there.

370
00:33:53,198 --> 00:33:56,034
I just couldn't picture

371
00:33:56,452 --> 00:33:58,620
going home together and

372
00:33:58,704 --> 00:34:01,165
feeling that passion again.

373
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:07,296
I've got nothing but gratitude.

374
00:34:16,597 --> 00:34:18,140
I feel a sense of clarity.

375
00:34:18,599 --> 00:34:21,643
Ever since my divorce,
I had been running away from

376
00:34:21,810 --> 00:34:24,271
the idea of dating or
putting myself out there.

377
00:34:24,688 --> 00:34:26,815
Just being able to say those words…

378
00:34:27,024 --> 00:34:29,693
I feel like I finally broke out of

379
00:34:29,777 --> 00:34:31,320
my shell.

380
00:34:31,528 --> 00:34:33,739
I'm so deeply thankful to Kaede for

381
00:34:33,822 --> 00:34:35,699
giving me that push.

382
00:34:36,033 --> 00:34:40,370
It was such a powerful wake-up call,
and I know I'll carry these lessons

383
00:34:40,454 --> 00:34:43,248
into my life moving forward.

384
00:34:43,999 --> 00:34:46,835
It truly was an incredible journey.

385
00:34:49,087 --> 00:34:52,299
This is so tough.

386
00:34:53,258 --> 00:34:56,428
But seeing those tears…

387
00:34:56,720 --> 00:34:59,181
you really feel the sheer resolve

388
00:34:59,389 --> 00:35:02,518
it took for them to
even step onto this show.

389
00:35:02,851 --> 00:35:05,646
Putting your heart on the line
for a confession

390
00:35:05,771 --> 00:35:09,233
takes a massive emotional toll.

391
00:35:09,483 --> 00:35:13,654
There's nothing quite like the heavy ache
of unrequited adult love.

392
00:35:13,821 --> 00:35:17,533
Seriously, I need some sugar right now
just to process this.

393
00:35:18,033 --> 00:35:19,284
That was so heavy.

394
00:35:19,368 --> 00:35:23,539
Is this really the kind of heartbreak
you endure as a grown adult?

395
00:35:23,789 --> 00:35:25,123
It feels so raw…

396
00:35:25,207 --> 00:35:28,168
Watching someone walk away
in front of you is brutal at any age.

397
00:35:28,252 --> 00:35:31,255
That kind of heartbreak
doesn't get easier with age.

398
00:35:37,761 --> 00:35:39,847
Yoko.

399
00:36:01,243 --> 00:36:02,953
Satoshi.

400
00:36:48,373 --> 00:36:51,084
Two busses.

401
00:37:19,112 --> 00:37:20,447
Alright.

402
00:37:29,039 --> 00:37:31,166
Good morning.

403
00:37:31,333 --> 00:37:32,876
Good morning. Please.

404
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:34,461
Sorry to keep you waiting.

405
00:37:34,544 --> 00:37:35,879
I've waited.

406
00:37:35,963 --> 00:37:36,797
You really did, huh?

407
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:38,006
I did.

408
00:37:49,476 --> 00:37:52,104
Thank you.

409
00:37:54,606 --> 00:37:57,275
I feel relieved.

410
00:37:57,359 --> 00:37:58,610
You feel relieved?

411
00:37:59,236 --> 00:38:01,029
Relieved?

412
00:38:02,447 --> 00:38:07,953
Back at dinner,

413
00:38:08,036 --> 00:38:10,580
when you brought up the age gap

414
00:38:10,872 --> 00:38:13,041
and asked how I felt about it…

415
00:38:14,126 --> 00:38:15,419
I thought…

416
00:38:17,170 --> 00:38:20,298
the truth is, that age difference is why

417
00:38:20,382 --> 00:38:23,552
I'm so drawn to you. That's your appeal.

418
00:38:24,803 --> 00:38:29,266
It's your life experience,
the sheer depth of who you are.

419
00:38:31,226 --> 00:38:32,185
I see.

420
00:38:32,269 --> 00:38:34,521
Yeah. And in that moment…

421
00:38:35,355 --> 00:38:38,775
when I casually asked what drives you,

422
00:38:38,942 --> 00:38:40,819
without hesitation, you said

423
00:38:40,902 --> 00:38:43,947
it was the happiness and smiles
of your employees.

424
00:38:44,281 --> 00:38:45,824
It reconfirmed for me that

425
00:38:45,991 --> 00:38:48,577
I fall deeply for women who put others…

426
00:38:48,827 --> 00:38:51,997
who put their team

427
00:38:52,164 --> 00:38:55,584
before themselves.

428
00:38:55,834 --> 00:38:59,337
Because that's how I've always
tried to live my own life, too.

429
00:38:59,504 --> 00:39:03,091
That was the exact moment my curiosity

430
00:39:03,175 --> 00:39:06,470
turned into certainty.

431
00:39:06,970 --> 00:39:08,972
I realized I was in love with you.

432
00:39:14,269 --> 00:39:20,192
Things I could never tell my parents,
or even my closest friends…

433
00:39:20,650 --> 00:39:22,694
I felt like

434
00:39:25,864 --> 00:39:29,701
I could open up to you about anything.

435
00:39:30,952 --> 00:39:32,788
I feel like

436
00:39:33,121 --> 00:39:34,122
you're the only person

437
00:39:34,206 --> 00:39:36,291
who will ever make me feel that way.

438
00:39:49,054 --> 00:39:52,599
I love you, Yoko.

439
00:39:56,645 --> 00:39:58,021
Thank you.

440
00:39:58,271 --> 00:39:59,898
I love you.

441
00:40:00,607 --> 00:40:02,526
Thank you.

442
00:40:02,943 --> 00:40:04,486
Thank you, too.

443
00:40:14,913 --> 00:40:21,002
Hearing you lay your feelings out
so directly…

444
00:40:21,086 --> 00:40:23,338
it really meant the world to me.

445
00:40:24,589 --> 00:40:28,343
But… I have this real fear of
romantic commitment.

446
00:40:29,136 --> 00:40:31,555
People's feelings change, you know?

447
00:40:32,472 --> 00:40:36,184
And at my age, all that baggage
and past heartbreak

448
00:40:36,351 --> 00:40:38,979
just gets in the way.

449
00:40:42,190 --> 00:40:45,819
I only let myself fall to a point

450
00:40:46,695 --> 00:40:50,824
where I can stay in control…

451
00:40:52,284 --> 00:40:54,411
where I won't get jealous or vulnerable.

452
00:40:54,828 --> 00:40:59,374
Because otherwise, the fear of
getting hurt is just overwhelming.

453
00:41:10,844 --> 00:41:12,762
That's really how it is.

454
00:41:21,354 --> 00:41:23,940
I'm genuinely so grateful to have met you.

455
00:41:24,024 --> 00:41:26,318
I'm grateful, too.

456
00:41:28,195 --> 00:41:29,571
Bye.

457
00:41:29,654 --> 00:41:31,239
I'll be waiting.

458
00:41:31,323 --> 00:41:32,324
Okay.

459
00:42:00,518 --> 00:42:01,978
Alright.

460
00:42:12,280 --> 00:42:13,406
You doing okay?

461
00:42:13,490 --> 00:42:14,699
Hey. Not too hot out here?

462
00:42:14,824 --> 00:42:16,326
Good to see you.

463
00:42:22,999 --> 00:42:26,419
I just wanted to

464
00:42:26,670 --> 00:42:29,381
hear your voice one last time.

465
00:42:31,258 --> 00:42:34,135
Up until now,
I had no idea what I should do,

466
00:42:35,262 --> 00:42:37,138
honestly.

467
00:42:37,222 --> 00:42:40,558
I kept thinking I'm not for you.

468
00:42:41,142 --> 00:42:43,853
I was constantly trying to figure out

469
00:42:43,979 --> 00:42:46,815
when to pack up my feelings and walk away.

470
00:42:48,441 --> 00:42:50,443
Sure, I took Kaede out

471
00:42:50,527 --> 00:42:54,781
on dates and everything, but…

472
00:42:56,157 --> 00:43:00,537
I realized this whole month was
just leading up to

473
00:43:00,829 --> 00:43:04,416
hearing your true words
in our final 1-on-1.

474
00:43:08,920 --> 00:43:11,548
I had a huge realization today.

475
00:43:11,923 --> 00:43:14,676
I used to think

476
00:43:14,884 --> 00:43:18,805
I was so frustrated with you because

477
00:43:19,014 --> 00:43:22,767
we were completely out of sync.

478
00:43:23,351 --> 00:43:24,311
But it wasn't your fault.

479
00:43:24,394 --> 00:43:27,939
You have your own great qualities.

480
00:43:28,148 --> 00:43:32,360
I was the one being petty
and small-minded.

481
00:43:32,485 --> 00:43:35,572
That's why I kept getting angry at you.

482
00:43:36,906 --> 00:43:40,368
I realized I'm the one who needs to
do some serious growing up.

483
00:43:40,869 --> 00:43:42,370
So… I'm sorry.

484
00:43:42,579 --> 00:43:44,039
I'm so sorry for everything.

485
00:43:44,122 --> 00:43:45,498
No, don't say that.

486
00:43:52,339 --> 00:43:53,757
Part of me hoped

487
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:55,133
you were hinting that

488
00:43:55,216 --> 00:43:56,676
maybe I had a chance.

489
00:44:05,310 --> 00:44:09,981
I was so incredibly selfish with you.

490
00:44:10,315 --> 00:44:12,359
I was way too honest,

491
00:44:12,901 --> 00:44:15,945
and I truly regret it.

492
00:44:16,071 --> 00:44:18,615
I mean that from the bottom of my heart.

493
00:44:18,740 --> 00:44:22,619
I've been reflecting heavily.
That's what I've been

494
00:44:22,702 --> 00:44:24,412
writing in my journal.

495
00:44:25,789 --> 00:44:28,166
I need to put in the work on myself.

496
00:44:28,249 --> 00:44:31,127
Just defaulting to "take me or leave me"…

497
00:44:31,211 --> 00:44:33,338
that lazy mindset

498
00:44:34,881 --> 00:44:40,387
doesn't cut it anymore.

499
00:44:45,058 --> 00:44:47,602
What completely stunned me was

500
00:44:47,852 --> 00:44:50,897
seeing you tear up and give me
a real, genuine apology.

501
00:44:51,106 --> 00:44:54,651
That was the moment I knew
you really had changed.

502
00:44:56,319 --> 00:44:58,071
Back then…

503
00:44:58,154 --> 00:45:00,115
I thought taking the easy way out

504
00:45:00,198 --> 00:45:02,617
and apologizing first was fixing things,

505
00:45:02,951 --> 00:45:06,037
just to avoid seeing you upset.

506
00:45:07,497 --> 00:45:13,086
It took us five or six years to
finally reach this real understanding.

507
00:45:13,420 --> 00:45:14,546
So…

508
00:45:14,671 --> 00:45:17,006
if we hadn't come here this past month…

509
00:45:17,090 --> 00:45:18,299
you know…

510
00:45:18,550 --> 00:45:21,177
Where would we even be?

511
00:45:22,095 --> 00:45:23,721
I'm truly glad I came.

512
00:45:23,805 --> 00:45:24,931
I'm so glad we did.

513
00:45:25,014 --> 00:45:25,890
I'm so glad I came here.

514
00:45:26,015 --> 00:45:27,475
Thank you so much for coming.

515
00:45:27,684 --> 00:45:29,436
Thank you for inviting me

516
00:45:29,644 --> 00:45:30,979
and for being so persistent.

517
00:45:31,062 --> 00:45:32,730
Thank you so much.

518
00:45:33,565 --> 00:45:37,485
You used to ask me all the time,
"Why do you even like me this much?"

519
00:45:37,569 --> 00:45:39,320
And…

520
00:45:39,529 --> 00:45:42,449
I'd tell you I didn't have an answer…

521
00:45:44,367 --> 00:45:46,119
I still can't

522
00:45:46,202 --> 00:45:48,997
give you some clean, logical explanation,

523
00:45:50,331 --> 00:45:55,003
but my belief has always been…

524
00:45:57,797 --> 00:46:00,925
real love doesn't need a reason.

525
00:46:06,681 --> 00:46:10,351
If we leave here together,
we'll have a great time.

526
00:46:10,977 --> 00:46:13,313
And if not…
I'll be rooting for you no matter what.

527
00:46:15,315 --> 00:46:16,983
Thank you.

528
00:46:17,275 --> 00:46:18,943
Thank you.

529
00:46:19,402 --> 00:46:20,820
Thank you so much.

530
00:46:20,904 --> 00:46:22,405
Same.

531
00:46:27,994 --> 00:46:30,246
Thank you.

532
00:46:30,622 --> 00:46:32,457
Thank you.

533
00:46:32,916 --> 00:46:35,210
I want to be in your life.

534
00:46:38,087 --> 00:46:39,631
Thank you.

535
00:46:40,006 --> 00:46:41,883
Bye.

536
00:47:10,245 --> 00:47:11,871
Come on… please board.

537
00:47:59,043 --> 00:48:01,045
Which bus? Left or right?

538
00:48:49,719 --> 00:48:51,054
It's Satoshi…

539
00:48:51,137 --> 00:48:53,806
Wow… he actually pulled it off.

540
00:49:58,454 --> 00:50:02,125
The old me would've been
bawling my eyes out right now.

541
00:50:03,459 --> 00:50:06,045
But I didn't cry…
or maybe I just couldn't.

542
00:50:07,380 --> 00:50:10,466
Part of me feels like
I was prepared for this.

543
00:50:13,594 --> 00:50:17,223
Not being able to see Yoko's smile

544
00:50:17,390 --> 00:50:21,227
or hear her voice anymore…
it hurts. It's lonely.

545
00:50:22,603 --> 00:50:29,235
But I came here determined to walk away
and accept it if it didn't work out.

546
00:50:30,236 --> 00:50:35,783
More than anything,
I feel like I gave it everything I had.

547
00:50:37,076 --> 00:50:41,414
Before this, I only ever focused on work.

548
00:50:41,831 --> 00:50:45,877
This experience showed me
sides of life I never would've seen.

549
00:50:46,794 --> 00:50:49,964
Honestly, I have nothing but gratitude.

550
00:50:59,640 --> 00:51:02,810
I'm here!

551
00:51:05,062 --> 00:51:07,815
Being direct made her happy.

552
00:51:08,024 --> 00:51:10,276
I guess being straightforward paid off.

553
00:51:10,610 --> 00:51:12,403
Sorry to keep you waiting.

554
00:51:13,446 --> 00:51:16,449
I'm way too embarrassed to
look at you right now.

555
00:51:17,867 --> 00:51:19,827
I'm here.

556
00:51:26,584 --> 00:51:32,089
I explained to Satoshi
why I could never do relationships…

557
00:51:32,965 --> 00:51:36,052
the constant fear of feelings fading,

558
00:51:36,135 --> 00:51:39,847
losing someone's love,

559
00:51:40,056 --> 00:51:43,100
and that core issue of

560
00:51:43,267 --> 00:51:45,728
never truly trusting people.

561
00:51:47,897 --> 00:51:52,109
I mean… how do I put this?

562
00:51:53,945 --> 00:51:59,283
We met through this hocance, but…

563
00:52:01,035 --> 00:52:05,122
Maybe it's out of line
for me to say this, but…

564
00:52:06,874 --> 00:52:10,169
Even if we hadn't met on this show…

565
00:52:10,253 --> 00:52:13,339
if we'd just met out in the real world,

566
00:52:13,631 --> 00:52:15,758
I know I still would've

567
00:52:17,009 --> 00:52:18,427
fallen for you.

568
00:52:23,349 --> 00:52:24,892
He told me that even if we hadn't

569
00:52:24,976 --> 00:52:27,478
met on this show,
he still would've fallen for me.

570
00:52:27,645 --> 00:52:29,939
That just meant so much to me…

571
00:52:30,022 --> 00:52:33,442
I completely broke down crying
right there out of pure joy.

572
00:52:35,319 --> 00:52:38,698
That moment was so romantic…

573
00:52:38,865 --> 00:52:41,492
it made me realize, this is what

574
00:52:41,701 --> 00:52:44,120
falling in love actually feels like.

575
00:52:46,622 --> 00:52:50,001
If you boarded, there was something
I wanted to give you.

576
00:52:50,084 --> 00:52:51,168
What is it?

577
00:52:54,255 --> 00:52:58,259
A photo of Tokyo Tower from our date.

578
00:52:59,302 --> 00:53:00,511
Let's put this up.

579
00:53:00,595 --> 00:53:03,347
Thank you, I love it.

580
00:53:03,639 --> 00:53:05,600
This is the one

581
00:53:05,683 --> 00:53:08,352
you said was your absolute favorite.

582
00:53:23,242 --> 00:53:27,496
Yoko and Satoshi are officially a couple!

583
00:53:27,663 --> 00:53:31,834
And while Hiroyoshi
put his heart on the line,

584
00:53:31,959 --> 00:53:35,755
Yoko didn't board his bus.

585
00:53:36,047 --> 00:53:38,215
I don't know what to believe anymore.

586
00:53:39,258 --> 00:53:41,093
That was a bit of a plot twist.

587
00:53:41,177 --> 00:53:44,013
Out of everyone this season,

588
00:53:44,096 --> 00:53:47,099
Satoshi was probably
the most direct and pure…

589
00:53:47,183 --> 00:53:48,392
I agree.

590
00:53:48,726 --> 00:53:53,439
…is what I thought.

591
00:53:53,522 --> 00:53:56,734
He had his messy moments early on,

592
00:53:56,817 --> 00:54:00,988
getting rowdy after drinking,

593
00:54:01,072 --> 00:54:04,742
but in the second half, his single-minded
devotion took center stage.

594
00:54:04,867 --> 00:54:06,619
Right.

595
00:54:06,869 --> 00:54:08,996
As for these two today,

596
00:54:09,330 --> 00:54:11,082
Yoko is based in Kobe

597
00:54:11,207 --> 00:54:14,085
and Satoshi is in Fukuoka.
They're doing long-distance.

598
00:54:14,168 --> 00:54:15,211
Them too.

599
00:54:15,503 --> 00:54:17,838
Yoko said, "I'd never actually put
effort into a relationship,"

600
00:54:17,922 --> 00:54:20,508
"so I was completely out of my depth."

601
00:54:20,800 --> 00:54:23,177
"We faced a major wall,
but communicated through it."

602
00:54:23,260 --> 00:54:25,721
"The difficult period is over now."

603
00:54:25,972 --> 00:54:28,474
"The act of putting effort into love
feels fresh to me."

604
00:54:28,641 --> 00:54:29,725
I see.

605
00:54:29,809 --> 00:54:32,645
Even after the show,
they had rough patches,

606
00:54:32,895 --> 00:54:34,063
but they powered through

607
00:54:34,146 --> 00:54:37,566
using the communication skills

608
00:54:37,775 --> 00:54:41,570
they built on Love Transit.
So glad for them.

609
00:55:40,337 --> 00:55:41,714
Good morning.

610
00:55:41,797 --> 00:55:43,299
Good morning.

611
00:55:57,146 --> 00:55:59,648
First off…

612
00:56:01,358 --> 00:56:06,405
Right up to the end,

613
00:56:07,782 --> 00:56:10,117
I fell right back into my old ways.

614
00:56:10,910 --> 00:56:14,955
Whenever something bothered me,
I'd just check out,

615
00:56:15,122 --> 00:56:19,168
shut down, and make it your problem.

616
00:56:19,460 --> 00:56:21,545
I'm so sorry for

617
00:56:23,422 --> 00:56:26,133
putting you through that

618
00:56:27,218 --> 00:56:29,386
right until the very last moment.

619
00:56:32,431 --> 00:56:37,311
Ever since we met,
I've been completely selfish

620
00:56:38,521 --> 00:56:42,483
and put you through so much pain.

621
00:56:43,776 --> 00:56:46,362
It was only after losing you

622
00:56:47,196 --> 00:56:50,533
that I realized just how massive
a space you held

623
00:56:51,242 --> 00:56:53,494
in my life.

624
00:56:54,203 --> 00:56:56,872
I know it seems like

625
00:56:57,998 --> 00:57:01,877
I keep flipping back and forth,
talking about

626
00:57:02,378 --> 00:57:04,255
moving abroad one minute,

627
00:57:04,338 --> 00:57:06,465
staying in Japan the next…

628
00:57:11,095 --> 00:57:13,514
but when I strip it all back

629
00:57:14,473 --> 00:57:18,227
and ask what matters,

630
00:57:18,561 --> 00:57:20,896
as long as I have you

631
00:57:21,438 --> 00:57:24,150
and the kids,

632
00:57:24,817 --> 00:57:27,278
I can…

633
00:57:30,072 --> 00:57:34,285
make it work anywhere.

634
00:57:35,661 --> 00:57:40,708
As for the issues you called me out on,

635
00:57:40,958 --> 00:57:46,755
I know those are things

636
00:57:49,466 --> 00:57:53,137
I can change.

637
00:57:56,682 --> 00:58:02,563
Out of everything you've ever said to me,

638
00:58:03,272 --> 00:58:05,983
what meant the most was

639
00:58:06,400 --> 00:58:08,235
when you said you wanted to

640
00:58:08,319 --> 00:58:10,905
keep building on your love for me.

641
00:58:13,741 --> 00:58:17,912
But spending this time together…

642
00:58:18,746 --> 00:58:21,874
at your core, nothing has changed.

643
00:58:21,999 --> 00:58:25,502
You haven't changed at all.

644
00:58:26,629 --> 00:58:28,631
I'm still the one

645
00:58:29,298 --> 00:58:32,801
who has to coax you

646
00:58:33,052 --> 00:58:37,431
and pull out your actual feelings…

647
00:58:37,848 --> 00:58:40,476
and part of me just wishes

648
00:58:40,809 --> 00:58:43,312
you'd meet me halfway for once.

649
00:58:45,856 --> 00:58:48,525
I need security.

650
00:58:49,276 --> 00:58:54,198
Sparks matter in romance, sure,

651
00:58:56,116 --> 00:58:58,661
but on a deeper level,

652
00:58:58,869 --> 00:59:02,706
I need you to give me peace of mind.

653
00:59:03,916 --> 00:59:07,127
If that core part of you hasn't changed,

654
00:59:07,711 --> 00:59:11,423
getting back together is
completely pointless.

655
00:59:13,008 --> 00:59:15,219
That's what's been

656
00:59:15,302 --> 00:59:17,888
weighing on me this whole time…

657
00:59:19,723 --> 00:59:22,643
and I needed to lay that out
before this ends.

658
00:59:29,233 --> 00:59:30,776
Before coming on this show,

659
00:59:32,611 --> 00:59:35,990
I felt like I didn't deserve love…

660
00:59:37,324 --> 00:59:41,203
like I didn't even deserve to
exist as a decent person.

661
00:59:41,870 --> 00:59:45,082
That's how I felt,

662
00:59:45,749 --> 00:59:49,128
but during this hocance,

663
00:59:49,795 --> 00:59:53,799
despite all my mess,
everyone still reached out to me.

664
00:59:54,883 --> 00:59:57,011
Watching them…

665
01:00:01,807 --> 01:00:03,684
I feel like I've started to change.

666
01:00:05,853 --> 01:00:09,606
Everyone here truly helped me grow up.

667
01:00:11,525 --> 01:00:13,152
I just…

668
01:00:15,404 --> 01:00:17,448
I don't want to

669
01:00:19,158 --> 01:00:21,327
break your heart ever again.

670
01:00:23,454 --> 01:00:25,164
So…

671
01:00:26,457 --> 01:00:32,087
I'm done using my usual cop-out…

672
01:00:32,421 --> 01:00:34,256
telling you that

673
01:00:35,466 --> 01:00:37,343
you'd be happier

674
01:00:40,846 --> 01:00:42,931
with someone else.

675
01:00:45,517 --> 01:00:48,312
I'm taking everything I learned here,

676
01:00:50,439 --> 01:00:52,149
and I'm going to

677
01:00:53,901 --> 01:00:55,486
make you

678
01:01:01,658 --> 01:01:03,744
and our family happy.

679
01:01:14,296 --> 01:01:16,632
Sorry, I…

680
01:01:17,216 --> 01:01:20,219
I really wanted to go big on this, but…

681
01:01:21,595 --> 01:01:23,472
you know money's tight for me now.

682
01:01:24,431 --> 01:01:26,058
Thank you.

683
01:01:26,433 --> 01:01:32,064
It's not much, but it's a gift that fits

684
01:01:32,898 --> 01:01:36,068
where I'm at right now.

685
01:01:38,987 --> 01:01:43,826
Alright, I should head to the bus.

686
01:01:44,535 --> 01:01:46,495
If I stay any longer,
I'm just gonna keep crying.

687
01:01:48,080 --> 01:01:49,623
Thanks.

688
01:01:52,543 --> 01:01:54,920
Thank you.

689
01:02:58,984 --> 01:03:00,652
Thank you.

690
01:03:05,699 --> 01:03:07,576
I'm so sorry… for everything, always.

691
01:03:20,047 --> 01:03:22,758
Honestly, I couldn't care less about this.

692
01:03:22,841 --> 01:03:24,343
This Hocance thing.

693
01:03:24,843 --> 01:03:28,972
I'd be fine packing up
and leaving right this second.

694
01:03:31,350 --> 01:03:36,313
So if the woman you need
to make amends with

695
01:03:36,396 --> 01:03:38,190
is calling for you…

696
01:03:38,440 --> 01:03:41,610
I just think, "Man,
you better step up and fight."

697
01:03:41,735 --> 01:03:44,905
"Don't you dare act like
a pathetic coward."

698
01:03:51,620 --> 01:03:52,579
Here you go.

699
01:03:52,663 --> 01:03:53,747
Oh, I already took one.

700
01:03:54,206 --> 01:03:55,874
I already took the picture.

701
01:03:58,669 --> 01:04:03,423
Right before the divorce, I asked our son…

702
01:04:03,757 --> 01:04:07,010
"If there were no rules or limits…"

703
01:04:09,137 --> 01:04:12,266
"what would you want most?"
And he told me,

704
01:04:14,518 --> 01:04:16,979
"I won't ask for much."

705
01:04:17,271 --> 01:04:19,815
"I just wish we could go back to
how we used to be."

706
01:04:43,213 --> 01:04:46,341
Honestly, I hated this experience
and just wanted to go home.

707
01:04:46,508 --> 01:04:49,678
That's just the kind of guy I am…

708
01:04:50,846 --> 01:04:52,889
and I was completely burnt out.

709
01:04:53,432 --> 01:04:58,604
But then, for the rest of my life…

710
01:05:03,358 --> 01:05:05,277
I wondered…

711
01:05:06,820 --> 01:05:09,448
if I'd ever…

712
01:05:19,333 --> 01:05:24,630
find people…

713
01:05:24,713 --> 01:05:31,720
I could actually open my heart to again.

714
01:05:33,055 --> 01:05:37,184
Thank you for

715
01:05:40,979 --> 01:05:44,274
accepting someone

716
01:05:47,569 --> 01:05:49,738
as broken as me

717
01:05:51,365 --> 01:05:52,991
as a true friend.

718
01:05:53,116 --> 01:05:55,202
Thank you all.

719
01:06:12,594 --> 01:06:13,804
Here.

720
01:06:21,019 --> 01:06:22,813
If you take me for granted,

721
01:06:24,898 --> 01:06:26,233
there will be hell to pay.

722
01:06:28,819 --> 01:06:30,404
You don't get a second chance.

723
01:06:31,446 --> 01:06:32,614
Got it?

724
01:06:34,116 --> 01:06:35,492
Yes.

725
01:06:41,540 --> 01:06:43,208
I'll make you happy.

726
01:06:45,377 --> 01:06:46,753
Good.

727
01:06:49,423 --> 01:06:50,924
Let's go home.

728
01:06:52,551 --> 01:06:53,927
Thank you.

729
01:06:57,973 --> 01:07:01,017
Let's come back to Okinawa
again with the kids.

730
01:07:02,018 --> 01:07:03,520
Yeah.

731
01:07:12,362 --> 01:07:14,072
And there it is…

732
01:07:14,948 --> 01:07:18,368
Mao and Hikaru are
officially back together!

733
01:07:18,493 --> 01:07:21,288
Honestly, what really hit me was

734
01:07:22,164 --> 01:07:25,125
how remarkably composed
Mao stayed right up to the end.

735
01:07:25,417 --> 01:07:28,712
Seriously, isn't Mao
just way too incredible of a woman?

736
01:07:28,879 --> 01:07:30,046
She's amazing.

737
01:07:30,130 --> 01:07:31,590
Amazing.

738
01:07:31,673 --> 01:07:32,966
Such a deep, forgiving heart.

739
01:07:33,175 --> 01:07:34,092
Now comes the real part.

740
01:07:34,176 --> 01:07:36,344
From here on out,

741
01:07:36,720 --> 01:07:38,054
it's really all for the kids.

742
01:07:38,138 --> 01:07:39,097
Right.

743
01:07:39,264 --> 01:07:41,600
It feels like the true test starts now.

744
01:07:41,933 --> 01:07:44,144
Honestly,

745
01:07:44,603 --> 01:07:46,438
watching all their weird antics early on,

746
01:07:46,521 --> 01:07:48,648
I never expected to
end up crying like this.

747
01:07:48,982 --> 01:07:51,276
It just felt like a wild show
full of eccentric antics.

748
01:07:51,485 --> 01:07:54,863
I really didn't expect to
shed actual tears.

749
01:07:54,946 --> 01:07:56,031
The emotional contrast…

750
01:07:56,156 --> 01:08:00,243
At first, I didn't think a single person
would walk away together.

751
01:08:00,327 --> 01:08:02,245
I thought, "What a bunch of weirdos."

752
01:08:02,996 --> 01:08:04,539
Like, what even is an adult?

753
01:08:04,790 --> 01:08:06,541
It gets you all philosophical.

754
01:08:06,625 --> 01:08:11,213
Watching this, I kept thinking
adults are really just big kids.

755
01:08:11,296 --> 01:08:12,798
When you hear what his kid said

756
01:08:12,881 --> 01:08:14,800
right as they got back together,

757
01:08:15,050 --> 01:08:16,468
it turns out the kids are the real adults.

758
01:08:16,551 --> 01:08:17,844
So true.

759
01:08:18,136 --> 01:08:21,139
It makes you question
who's really the mature one here.

760
01:08:21,223 --> 01:08:23,266
Sometimes the kids see things
clearer than we do.

761
01:08:23,391 --> 01:08:25,894
It really leaves you with a lot to ponder.

762
01:08:25,977 --> 01:08:27,938
I really hope the four who ended up single

763
01:08:28,104 --> 01:08:29,773
find their own happiness, too.

764
01:08:29,856 --> 01:08:31,608
Yes, I hope so too.

765
01:08:31,733 --> 01:08:33,860
I just want everyone to be happy.

766
01:08:34,110 --> 01:08:36,238
And with that,

767
01:08:36,446 --> 01:08:38,615
thank you all for riding along with us.

768
01:08:38,698 --> 01:08:41,201
It's been an absolute blast.

769
01:08:41,284 --> 01:08:42,452
Thank you.

770
01:08:42,536 --> 01:08:44,538
Here's hoping we'll see you all again

771
01:08:44,621 --> 01:08:46,873
for Season 2 of Love Transit 35+!

772
01:08:46,957 --> 01:08:49,501
Thank you so much, everyone!

773
01:08:49,584 --> 01:08:52,254
Thank you!
